class:: BlipDiff
summary:: Bound-normalized phase derivative of a finite Blip
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/BlipExtensions, Classes/BlipAD, Classes/BlipDecay, Classes/BlipDisp, Classes/BlipFB, Classes/BlipFrac, Classes/BlipInt, Classes/BlipKernel, Classes/BlipPM, Classes/BlipPeak, Classes/BlipPower, Classes/BlipSeries, Classes/BlipWidth

description::

BlipDiff evaluates code::-sum(k * sin(k * phase)):: and divides by
code::sum(k)::. It is antisymmetric, zero mean, and emphasizes high harmonics.
Normalization is by a mathematical magnitude bound, so output amplitude does
not scale with frequency.

A differentiated geometric-series form gives constant cost in harmonic
count. Near phase wrap, a power-series limit avoids cancellation. Effective
count changes fade over one block. Only the retained carrier harmonics are
present, and they are limited below the Nyquist safety margin.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/Blip::. BlipDiff has the same
retained harmonic locations, but their magnitudes rise in proportion to
harmonic index and their phases are differentiated.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Frequency in Hz. Audio or control rate; signed values are valid.

argument:: numharm
Requested harmonic count, sampled once per block and clipped to code::1..2048::
before Nyquist limiting.

argument:: mul
Post-processing multiplier.

argument:: add
Post-processing offset.

examples::

code::
(
{ BlipDiff.ar(100, 40, 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{ Ringz.ar(BlipDiff.ar(6, 80), 1800, 0.08) * 0.1 }.play;
)
::

code::
// Modulating all parameters for a dynamic sound
(
{ BlipDiff.ar(LFNoise1.kr(1).exprange(100, 800), SinOsc.kr(0.2).range(1, 100)) ! 2 * 0.1 }.play;
)
::
